C = {}
UAE = dict(country='United Arab Emirates', cc='AE')
IN = dict(country='India', cc='IN')

C['marketing-agency-dubai.html'] = dict(city='Dubai', **UAE, region='AE-DU', kind='marketing', hub='marketing.html', cityhub='/dubai/',
 title='Marketing Agency in Dubai | Strategy, Ads & Content',
 desc='Marketing agency and consultant in Dubai: brand strategy, Meta and Google ads, social media and content shot in-house for hospitality, property, retail.',
 h1='Marketing Agency', h1em='in Dubai', imgs='mkt',
 sections=[
  ('Marketing for a city that runs on visuals', ['Dubai is one of the most visually competitive markets anywhere. Hotels, restaurants, developers, beauty clinics and retail brands all compete for the same scroll, often with big production budgets. A marketing plan here has to assume your content will sit next to the best in the world, and your audience is international: residents from dozens of countries, tourists and investors who often find you on Instagram or Google Maps before anything else.',
   'YKS Productions works as a compact marketing agency for Dubai brands. I set the strategy, plan the channels and shoot the content myself. My background includes campaign and content work for Marriott and Vaseline (Unilever), and a campaign reel that reached 3.3 million views. You deal directly with the person doing the work.']),
  ('What Dubai clients usually need', ['<strong>Hospitality and F&amp;B</strong>: Instagram and TikTok reels, Google Business Profile, Meta ads around launches and seasonal offers. <strong>Real estate</strong>: listing films, developer launch campaigns, lead forms on Meta and search campaigns on Google for project names. <strong>Beauty, wellness and clinics</strong>: trust-building content, UGC-style testimonials (with consent) and search ads for treatments. <strong>Founders and consultants</strong>: LinkedIn personal branding for a business audience across the GCC.']),
  ('Bilingual and multicultural audiences', ['Many Dubai campaigns need to work for English- and Arabic-speaking audiences, as well as for large South Asian and European communities. I plan creative that relies on visuals and simple on-screen text first, so it travels across audiences, and work with your translators or Arabic copywriters where campaigns need native-language versions.']),
  ('On the ground across Dubai', ['Shoots across Downtown, Business Bay, DIFC, Dubai Marina, JLT, Palm Jumeirah, Jumeirah, Al Quoz studios and newer communities in Dubai South and Dubailand. Strategy sessions in person or online.'])],
 faqs=[('Are you a full marketing agency in Dubai?','A compact one. Strategy, ads and content production are handled by me directly, and specialists are brought in for things like Arabic copywriting or drones when a project needs them.'),
  ('Which ad platforms work best in Dubai?','Instagram and Meta ads for hospitality, beauty and lifestyle; Google Search for high-intent services; LinkedIn for B2B. Most Dubai brands benefit from Meta plus Google.'),
  ('Can you help with Google Maps visibility?','Yes. Google Business Profile setup and optimisation, fresh photos, posts and a review-request process are part of local SEO.'),
  ('How do quotes work?','Monthly retainers or project fees based on scope. You get one written quote before work starts.')],
 blog='blog/meta-ads-vs-google-ads-dubai.html')

C['marketing-agency-abu-dhabi.html'] = dict(city='Abu Dhabi', **UAE, region='AE-AZ', kind='marketing', hub='marketing.html', cityhub='/photographer-abu-dhabi.html',
 title='Marketing Agency in Abu Dhabi | Strategy & Content',
 desc='Marketing consultant for Abu Dhabi brands: brand strategy, digital marketing, Meta, Google and LinkedIn ads, and photo and video content shot on location.',
 h1='Marketing Agency', h1em='in Abu Dhabi', imgs='brand',
 sections=[
  ('A quieter, more considered market', ['Abu Dhabi rewards credibility more than noise. The capital&rsquo;s economy leans on government-linked entities, culture and tourism, hospitality on Yas and Saadiyat islands, real estate communities like Al Reem, Al Raha and Saadiyat, and a growing start-up and tech scene around Hub71 and ADGM. Marketing that works here tends to be polished, respectful and clear rather than loud.',
   'I help Abu Dhabi businesses build that credibility: sharp positioning, a professional content library, and campaigns aimed at the right people. Content is shot by me on a Sony A7 IV, so your brand looks consistent everywhere it appears.']),
  ('Where I focus in Abu Dhabi', ['<strong>Hospitality and attractions</strong>: content and paid social that reach both residents and visitors from Dubai and abroad. <strong>Real estate</strong>: launch content and lead generation for off-plan and ready communities. <strong>B2B and professional services</strong>: LinkedIn marketing and founder-led content for firms in ADGM and the wider business community. <strong>Education and healthcare</strong>: trust-first content and search campaigns for enquiries.']),
  ('Working between Abu Dhabi and Dubai', ['Many brands sell across both emirates. I plan campaigns that target each city&rsquo;s audience separately where it matters, for example different location targeting and creative for Abu Dhabi residents versus weekend visitors from Dubai, and combine shoot days to keep production efficient.']),
  ('Locations', ['Corniche, Saadiyat Island, Yas Island, Al Reem Island, Al Maryah Island, Al Raha Beach, Khalifa City and Masdar City. Strategy and reporting run online between visits.'])],
 faqs=[('Do you travel to Abu Dhabi for shoots?','Yes. Shoot days are planned on location in Abu Dhabi; strategy and campaign management run remotely.'),
  ('Do you work with government entities?','I work with businesses of all types, but I don&rsquo;t claim government clients I haven&rsquo;t had. Past brands include Marriott, Vaseline (Unilever), KL Rahul and Cindrebay School of Design.'),
  ('Can campaigns target only Abu Dhabi?','Yes. Meta, Google and LinkedIn all allow location targeting at emirate or city level.'),
  ('Do you create Arabic content?','I produce the visuals and work with your Arabic copywriter or translator for native-language versions.')],
 blog='blog/meta-ads-vs-google-ads-dubai.html')

C['marketing-agency-bangalore.html'] = dict(city='Bangalore', **IN, region='IN-KA', kind='marketing', hub='marketing.html', cityhub='/india/',
 title='Marketing Agency in Bangalore | Brand, Ads & Content',
 desc='Marketing agency in Bangalore for startups, SaaS and D2C brands: brand strategy, performance marketing, LinkedIn, social media and content shot in-house.',
 h1='Marketing Agency', h1em='in Bangalore', imgs='ads',
 sections=[
  ('Marketing for India&rsquo;s startup capital', ['Bangalore is full of companies that build excellent products and then struggle to explain them. SaaS and B2B tech, deep-tech startups, D2C brands, ed-tech, cafes and restaurants, and a fast-moving real estate market in areas like Whitefield, Sarjapur and North Bangalore. The common challenge is clarity: telling a busy buyer what you do and why it matters in a few seconds.',
   'I work with Bangalore teams on exactly that. Brand strategy and messaging first, then the channels and content to carry it. Being a photographer, videographer and content creator with 8 years of experience means the strategy comes with the production capability built in.']),
  ('Typical Bangalore engagements', ['<strong>B2B and SaaS</strong>: positioning, LinkedIn personal branding for founders, LinkedIn and Google Search ads, product explainer videos and case-study content. <strong>D2C brands</strong>: Meta ads with a steady supply of reels, UGC and product photography, plus creator partnerships. <strong>Hospitality and food</strong>: Instagram content and local SEO for cafes, breweries and restaurants in Indiranagar, Koramangala and HSR Layout. <strong>Real estate</strong>: project films and lead generation.']),
  ('Startup-friendly ways of working', ['Startups move fast and budgets are watched closely. I scope work in clear phases: a positioning sprint, a content shoot, then a monthly engagement once there&rsquo;s proof it works. Everything lives in your own accounts, so nothing is lost if the team changes.']),
  ('Around the city', ['Shoots and meetings across Indiranagar, Koramangala, HSR Layout, MG Road, UB City, Whitefield, Electronic City, Hebbal and Yelahanka.'])],
 faqs=[('Do you work with early-stage startups?','Yes. A focused positioning sprint and one content shoot is often the right first step before a retainer.'),
  ('Can you run LinkedIn ads for a Bangalore SaaS company?','Yes, alongside founder-led content on LinkedIn and Google Search for high-intent keywords.'),
  ('Do you handle Kannada content?','Creative is mostly English-led; for Kannada or Hindi versions I work with native copywriters.'),
  ('How are you different from a Bangalore digital agency?','You work directly with the person who plans and shoots. No hand-offs between strategy and production.')],
 blog='blog/brand-video-cost-bangalore.html')

C['marketing-agency-mumbai.html'] = dict(city='Mumbai', **IN, region='IN-MH', kind='marketing', hub='marketing.html', cityhub='/india/',
 title='Marketing Agency in Mumbai | Brand Strategy & Ads',
 desc='Marketing consultant in Mumbai for fashion, beauty, D2C and finance brands: brand strategy, Meta and Google ads, creator marketing and content production.',
 h1='Marketing Agency', h1em='in Mumbai', imgs='social',
 sections=[
  ('Standing out in India&rsquo;s media capital', ['Mumbai is where Indian advertising, film and fashion meet. Audiences here have seen it all, so brands compete on taste and storytelling as much as budget. The city&rsquo;s strongest categories (fashion and beauty, D2C consumer brands, BFSI and fintech, hospitality and real estate) all depend on sharp creative.',
   'My experience on Malayalam feature film sets (Soothravakyam, Baby Girl) and brand work for Vaseline (Unilever) and Marriott translates well to Mumbai&rsquo;s expectations: cinematic content, a clear brand idea and campaigns built around them.']),
  ('What Mumbai brands ask for', ['<strong>Fashion and beauty</strong>: lookbooks, reels, creator collaborations and Meta ads. <strong>D2C</strong>: a steady flow of ad creative and UGC to keep Meta campaigns fresh. <strong>Finance and fintech</strong>: brand trust content, explainer videos and LinkedIn for leadership. <strong>Hospitality and real estate</strong>: films and campaigns for launches in areas like Bandra, Worli and Powai.']),
  ('Creator and influencer marketing in Mumbai', ['Mumbai has India&rsquo;s densest creator ecosystem. I help brands brief creators clearly, choose them on audience fit rather than follower count, secure the usage rights needed to reuse content in ads, and measure results with codes and links.']),
  ('Working in Mumbai', ['Shoot days in Bandra, Juhu, Andheri, Lower Parel, BKC, Colaba, Worli and Powai, planned around travel. Strategy, ads and reporting run remotely.'])],
 faqs=[('Do you have a Mumbai office?','No. I travel to Mumbai for shoot days and run strategy and campaigns remotely, which keeps costs lean.'),
  ('Can you help with influencer marketing in Mumbai?','Yes: briefs, shortlisting, usage rights and content planning.'),
  ('Which brands have you worked with?','Vaseline (Unilever), Marriott, KL Rahul and Cindrebay School of Design, plus film stills work on Soothravakyam and Baby Girl.'),
  ('Do you do personal branding for Mumbai founders?','Yes. I wrote a guide on it: LinkedIn personal branding for founders in Mumbai.')],
 blog='blog/linkedin-personal-branding-founders-mumbai.html')

C['marketing-agency-delhi.html'] = dict(city='Delhi NCR', **IN, region='IN-DL', kind='marketing', hub='marketing.html', cityhub='/india/',
 title='Marketing Agency in Delhi NCR | Ads, Brand & Content',
 desc='Marketing consultant for Delhi, Gurugram and Noida: brand strategy, Google and Meta ads, LinkedIn marketing, social media and content production.',
 h1='Marketing Agency', h1em='in Delhi NCR', imgs='linkedin',
 sections=[
  ('One region, three very different markets', ['Delhi NCR is really three markets. Gurugram is corporate: MNC offices, consulting firms and fast-growing startups along Cyber City and Golf Course Road. Noida has media houses, IT services and a large education sector. Delhi itself has some of India&rsquo;s strongest fashion designers, premium hospitality, and a huge wedding and events economy. Marketing that works in one doesn&rsquo;t always work in the others.',
   'I plan campaigns with that in mind, targeting by area and audience, and producing content that fits the category: polished corporate video for Gurugram, fashion-led visuals for South Delhi brands, lead-generation for education and services.']),
  ('Common Delhi NCR engagements', ['<strong>Corporate and B2B</strong>: LinkedIn marketing, leadership personal branding and corporate video. <strong>Education and coaching</strong>: Google Search and Meta lead generation with landing pages and clear tracking. <strong>Fashion and design labels</strong>: lookbooks, reels and Meta ads. <strong>Hospitality, events and weddings</strong>: content that shows atmosphere and craft.']),
  ('Lead generation done carefully', ['Lead-heavy sectors in NCR often suffer from low-quality leads. I set up qualifying questions on forms, conversion tracking that feeds back to the platforms, and simple reporting so you can see cost per real enquiry, not just cost per form fill.']),
  ('Across NCR', ['Shoot days in Connaught Place, Hauz Khas, Saket, Mehrauli, Vasant Kunj, Gurugram Cyber City, Golf Course Road and Noida, planned around travel.'])],
 faqs=[('Do you cover Gurugram and Noida?','Yes, all of Delhi NCR.'),
  ('Can you run Google Ads for an education business?','Yes, with conversion tracking and lead qualification so you can judge quality, not just volume.'),
  ('Do you shoot corporate video in Gurugram?','Yes: company profiles, leadership messages and recruitment videos. See video production.'),
  ('How do we start?','A short discovery call, then a written proposal with scope and price.')],
 blog='blog/marketing-agency-vs-consultant-india.html')

